  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1232 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nShowers and storms will gradually end from west to east on Monday \nnight as shortwave energy lifts away from the region. Flow aloft \nwill then weaken and become more zonal, resulting in a period of \ndrier and warmer weather on Tuesday and Wednesday with temperatures \nrising back near or just above seasonal normals. During the late \nweek period, models still highlight a return to a more active \npattern as longwave troughing develops over the eastern Pacific and \nadjacent western CONUS. This will allow moist southwest flow aloft \nto persist over our area, with the pattern favorable for several \ndisturbances to track overhead. At this point, ensemble consensus \nstrongly favors the period from late Thursday through early Saturday \nfor widespread precipitation, but any other details are still murky \nat this lead time.",
